---
permalink: /_redirects
layout: null
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
# Built from collections.all, so every page Eleventy writes gets a line.
# Pages build to flat files (stack.html) and Netlify serves /stack from them.
# These send the old .html addresses, which are linked from outside, to the
# clean URL with a 301 so search engines see one page, not two. The `!`
# forces the rule even though stack.html exists; without it Netlify serves
# the file and skips the redirect. The home page's url is already "/", so
# the loop skips it and it gets its own line.
/index.html  /  301!
{%- for entry in collections.all %}
{%- set clean = entry.url | cleanUrl %}
{%- if clean != entry.url %}
{{ entry.url }}  {{ clean }}  301!
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
